**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`

**How to implement.** AT-1 builds the optics-mueller kit (001 §1a; 001 §Q 'Common rules' 'Build: each test builds its kit ONLY through the semantic messages (§P), against a SQLite `:memory:` library, and writes it through the REAL folder `KitProxy` into a throw-away folder under the test run's output directory'; .spec-md §3.13). The class is the kit-acceptance gate's (001 §U; `.gates/OpticalConstructor/kit-acceptance.gates`, which runs `--filter-trait "Category=kit-acceptance"` in this project and which `ui-tests` excludes); from this step on it runs on every step that touches the study, the run law, the import code, this file or the kits. It follows `FsxAcceptanceTests`' pattern (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:runOnTable`): the app's own update functions (`updateKitStart`, step 176; `updateTableAndElementRotation`) fold the same semantic messages the controls send, and nothing is clicked. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S12.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs` (steps 83, 152, 154, 414): `inverseModelOver (context : AppContext) (opened : OpenedKit) : TableAndElementRotationModel`, with a one-line doc, is the Inverse model `studyKitIn` builds today (step 414: `initInverse` over the context's stores overlaid with `opened.overlay`, `loadKit opened`, and the item models and catalogue imports the window's seed threads, steps 154, 243); `studyKitIn` calls it in place of its own body, so one composition exists (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy') and `StudyViewTests` keeps its assertions. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs`, `module KitAcceptanceTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment (the project references `BerremanTestSupport` since step 347). Its module doc, one to three lines: AT-1 and AT-2 build the two reference kits through the app's messages and prove them against the committed kits (001 §Q; spec 0050 S12). Every fact carries `[<Trait("Category", "kit-acceptance")>]`. (3) The build, a private function of the module that later steps extend and every AT-1 fact calls: `buildOpticsMuellerKit (run : FolderName)` answers the built folder, the app context, the window model and the test clock, in this order. (a) The folder is `<System.AppContext.BaseDirectory>/KitAcceptanceTests/<run>/optics-mueller`, created fresh, its leaf naming the kit (step 145's `namedKitFile`); the committed kit's `data/` tree (`CommittedKit.OpticsMuellerKit.tryFindFolder`, `BerremanTestSupport/CommittedKits.fs`, steps 330, 344; .spec-md §3.21) is copied into it byte for byte, and nothing else. (b) The context is `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "KitAcceptanceTests")`, a SQLite `:memory:` library filled from `Catalogue/Builtin` (steps 83, 100). (c) The clock is a test-local `ClockProvider` over a mutable cell holding `ClockTime` of 2026-05-31T12:00:00Z (UTC), which only the build advances (step 427), so every stamp the kit stores is fixed. (d) New kit: a `KitStartModel` from `initKitStart` over a `KitStartContext` of `KitHistoryProxy.createInMemory ()`, `KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue`, the test clock, `kitIds` answering `KitId (Guid.Parse "e63c9d6e-7961-4d9f-9c8d-e5a151414e0e")` (step 420), `KitAuthor "optics-mueller lab"`, `context.catalogueImports`, `TestAppScope.kitPickerOf` the folder, a `showKit` that keeps the opened kit, `activateKitWindow` answering `NoKitWindowOpen`, `KitZipPicker.none`, `KitArchiveProxy.create ()` and `KitArchiveJobHost.inert`; `CreateKit` of the folder initialises it around its lab files (001 §F 'a folder that already has files keeps them'). The window model is `TestAppScope.inverseModelOver context <the opened kit>`, whose `itemIds` is replaced by a test-local `ItemIdProvider` answering, call by call, Laser `d4d8dfc0-3d43-4a24-853c-369479de4f5d`, LP1 `375bde88-fe45-4bd7-ad77-f13708076224`, LP2 `72d0505d-8685-4884-89ad-ea13694c8693`, CPL1 `0d2c2b6e-c91f-486b-b80b-a1b815c03aac`, CPL2 `b9f73589-6cfe-46d2-a5eb-2b11d6d6cd5f`, AIR `dc89cf47-6d94-4887-a0fb-49e3a8ca1cb4`, QZ `436f47ea-a1c4-47ed-8c5c-f09eae8098b1`, LR `69c2edf9-3a4d-4b23-bea2-94ba305ca507`, Phone `93fae6cc-d838-45b7-b5f0-949f7a759e91`. (e) The lab naming template: `SetNamingTemplateText (ControlCaption "{source:LP1=LP,CPL1=CPL}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer:LP2=LP,CPL2=CPL}-{note}")` and `SaveNamingTemplate` (step 273): `NamingTemplate.standard`'s placeholders (step 267) with the aliases that write the lab's parts `LP` and `CPL` for the items labelled `LP1`, `CPL1`, `LP2` and `CPL2` (step 268), because item labels are unique (001 §I) while the lab's names are not. (f) The nine items, each through `OpenAddItemForm`, `ChooseNewItemModel` of the form's offer, `SetNewItemLabel`, `SetNewItemDial` and `AddItem` of the form's draft (step 239), in this order: `Laser`, the `PresetIds.heNe633` source preset (the bench's red laser; a black-box reconstruction does not read the wavelength); `LP1` and `LP2`, the real linear polarizer (`ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId`); `CPL1` and `CPL2`, the circular polarizer (`circularPolarizerModelId`, a linear polarizer then a retarder at 45° plus its offset, step 210); `AIR`, the empty slot (`emptySlotModelId`); `QZ` and `LR`, the black-box Mueller model (`blackBoxMuellerModelId`); `Phone`, the intensity detector (`intensityDetectorModelId`). `LP2` is `DialMounted DialNegative` and `CPL2` `DialMounted DialPositive` (the reference's analyzer conventions, `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/matrix_glue.py:185-189`); every other item is `FixedMounting`. Then `SetParameterState` (step 240) sets the unknowns, each an `UnknownParameter` with no prior and its start and bounds in the parameter's own unit (`Angle.parameterValue`, step 389): `LP2`'s `dialZero` from 152° within [0°, 360°] and `CPL2`'s from 80° within [0°, 360°] (the lab's mounting readings, optics-mueller `AGENTS.md`); `CPL2`'s and `CPL1`'s `c2.retardance` from 90° within [0°, 180°]; `CPL1`'s `c2.fastAxisOffset` from 0° within [−45°, 45°]; and each of `QZ`'s and `LR`'s sixteen `m<r><c>` (`ParameterName.muellerElement`, step 244) from its default within [−2, 2]. Every other parameter keeps its known default (the `Phone`'s `gain` 1 and `darkOffset` 0). (g) The table: the Inverse table's `src`, `sample` and `det` slots plus, through the table's own messages (`AddElement`, then the Move bay's along-beam messages where a slot's default place is not its light-order place), a polarizer slot before `sample`, a second sample slot after it and a polarizer slot after that, so `Setup.lightOrder` (step 257) reads Source, Prep 1, Obj 1, Obj 2, Analyzer 1, Detector 1; `AssignSlot` (step 263) puts `Laser` in Source and `Phone` in Detector 1. (h) The setups, by the grid generator (steps 274, 281, 282; 001 §J), the Experiments draft holding no capture so the grids record setups alone (step 276): grid one toggles `LP1` and `CPL1` on Prep 1, `AIR`, `QZ` and `LR` on Obj 1 with the angles 0°, 45° and 90° (`AddSetupGridAngle`), and `LP2` and `CPL2` on Analyzer 1, unticks the combinations of `AIR` at 45° and 90° (`ToggleSetupGridCombination`) and sends `GenerateSetupGrid model.setupGrid`; grid two (after `CloseSetupGrid` and `OpenSetupGrid`) toggles `LP1` and `CPL1`, `QZ` on Obj 1 and `LR` on Obj 2, each object at 0°, 45° and 90°, and both analyzers, unticks every combination whose two object angles differ, and generates. The template names them (001 §J 'two-sample setups put QZ in Object 1 and LR in Object 2'), forty in all: `LP-(AIR#0)-LP`, `LP-(QZ#0)-LP`, `LP-(QZ#45)-LP`, `LP-(QZ#90)-LP`, `LP-(LR#0)-LP`, `LP-(LR#45)-LP`, `LP-(LR#90)-LP`, `LP-(QZ#0-LR#0)-LP`, `LP-(QZ#45-LR#45)-LP`, `LP-(QZ#90-LR#90)-LP`, `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `LP-(QZ#0)-CPL`, `LP-(QZ#45)-CPL`, `LP-(QZ#90)-CPL`, `LP-(LR#0)-CPL`, `LP-(LR#45)-CPL`, `LP-(LR#90)-CPL`, `LP-(QZ#0-LR#0)-CPL`, `LP-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL`, `LP-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP`, `CPL-(QZ#0)-LP`, `CPL-(QZ#45)-LP`, `CPL-(QZ#90)-LP`, `CPL-(LR#0)-LP`, `CPL-(LR#45)-LP`, `CPL-(LR#90)-LP`, `CPL-(QZ#0-LR#0)-LP`, `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-LP`, `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-LP`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#0)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL`, `CPL-(LR#0)-CPL`, `CPL-(LR#45)-CPL`, `CPL-(LR#90)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#0-LR#0)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL`. Then the two setups the LR correction re-points to (001 §1a 'LR was labelled +45/+90 but physically sat at −45/−90'; step 424): `ActivateSetup` of `CPL-(LR#90)-CPL`, its Obj 1 slot's R1 set to −90° through the Rotate bay's messages, `SetSetupName (ControlCaption "CPL-(LR#-90)-CPL")` and `CreateSetup` (step 260); and the same from `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL` with Obj 2 at −90° as `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#-90)-CPL`. Every write goes through the window's kit, which is `KitProxy.create` of the folder (step 126). (4) The fact `AT-1 builds the optics-mueller kit's items and setups through the app's messages`: after the build, a second `KitProxy.create` of the built folder reads `.kit-json` holding the id `e63c9d6e-7961-4d9f-9c8d-e5a151414e0e`, the name `optics-mueller`, the author `optics-mueller lab`, created and modified at 2026-05-31T12:00:00Z, the lab template, no import profile and no send exclusion; `readItems` the nine items with their ids, labels, models, dials, revision 1 and the unknowns above; `readSetups` exactly the forty-two setups named above, each in light order Source `Laser`, Prep 1 `LP1` or `CPL1` as its name's source part says, its objects and angles as its name says (the two corrected ones with LR at −90°), Analyzer 1 `LP2` or `CPL2`, Detector 1 `Phone`; every file under `library/` byte-identical to the built-in entry file of its id and version (`Catalogue/Builtin/`), the six entries the items instantiate among them; and every file under `data/` byte-identical to the committed kit's. Each assertion's message names the file and both values.

**Acceptance.** After AT-1's first part lands, `KitAcceptanceTests` MUST build the optics-mueller kit around a copy of the committed lab files through the start screen's and the kit window's messages alone, its kit file, nine items and forty-two setups as specified, and `studyKitIn` MUST build its model through `TestAppScope.inverseModelOver`; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, including `AT-1 builds the optics-mueller kit's items and setups through the app's messages`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected class, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.
